course: dictionary
lesson: 285
title: The amoeba: one cell, no fixed shape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An amoeba is a living thing so small that its whole body is just one cell. You cannot see it well with your eyes alone; you need a microscope. Even so, it is alive: it moves, it feeds, and it lives in ponds, soil and water.
explain: «An amoeba moves by flowing its inside forward into a bulge called a false foot, and it swallows food by flowing around it.» The false foot is also called a pseudopod. Because the amoeba has no fixed shape, its body changes as it moves.
explain: Think of an amoeba as a blob of jelly, not a creature with a set body. When it finds food, it does not bite. It wraps round the food and takes it in. The words around a new word, like «flowing» and «wraps round», tell you what it means.
fact: An amoeba is a single-celled organism: one cell does everything it needs to live.
fact: The plural of amoeba can be amoebas or amoebae; in the US it is often spelled ameba.
fact: An amoeba has no fixed shape, so «amoeba-like» means shapeless.
fact: Some kinds of amoeba can make you ill if you drink dirty water, which is why we boil or clean water first.
fact: «Pseudopods» are parts of an amoeba that push out, like fingers, to move and to catch food.
exercise: «An amoeba moves by flowing its inside forward into a bulge called a false foot.» What is another name for a false foot? | Cell | *Pseudopod | Microscope | Paramecium
exercise: How do you usually see an amoeba? | Through a telescope pointed at the sky | *With a microscope | By touching it with your fingers | With your bare eyes on a sunny day
exercise: What does «amoeba-like» mean? | Hard and bony | *Shapeless | Shaped like a fish | Very large and heavy
test: An amoeba eats by doing what? | *Wrapping round its food | Waiting in the sun until food comes | Biting its food with teeth | Swimming away from its food
test: «Amoebas flow like blobs of what?» Read the sentence: «Put one drop of pond water under a school microscope and a whole hidden world swims into view: slipper-shaped paramecia rowing with tiny hairs, amoebas flowing like blobs of jelly.» | *Jelly | Wood | Stone | Sand
exam: Why should we boil or clean water before drinking it? | To make it taste sweet | To stop the water from freezing | To make amoebas grow bigger | *Some amoebas in dirty water can cause illness
